  "bench_wording: the form of the spoken lines (LLMDialogClient's generation methods, through the production PromptBuilder and prompts.yaml), in English and Spanish. Reported in E0a, never a selection criterion: no case is critical.",
  "Fields: prompt (which line: generate_response, opening, resume_opening, ask_confirmation, response_to_intent, ask_cancel_confirmation, cancel_confirmed_response, quiz_feedback, quiz_summary, understanding_confirmed, procedure_summary, qa_opening) and its inputs as the skill builds them (task, slot_schema, frame_filled, history, user_text, extracted; question, expected, given; correct, total, wrongs; completed, not_done).",
  "The expectations: asks (true: the line must end in a question; false: a closing, no question at all; null: not checked), slot_kind (single | list: the slot the line asks for; null: none), max_words (the length limit the prompt states; null: none), slot_phrases (literal renderings of the internal slot names that must not be spoken; the slot names with an underscore are added by the benchmark), third_person (phrases that refer to the user in the third person).",
  "Each case: id, language (en | es), description (English), category.",
  "The situations are invented: no case may share content with an evaluation scenario (evaluation/experiments/scenarios), with a phase A case (datasets/phase_a) or with a quoted example of config/prompts.yaml; check with: python3 -m core.dataset_check."
 ],
